        "content": "# Technical Design: YAML Validator Command\n\n**Feature ID**: yaml-validator-command\n**Version**: 1.0.0\n**Created**: 2026-03-08\n**Status**: Draft\n\n---\n\n## 1. Design Overview\n\nA CLI command that validates YAML files for syntactic correctness, implemented entirely with Bun built-ins and hand-written TypeScript. The tool reads a file path from CLI arguments, parses the content through a custom YAML syntax validator, and reports success or failure with appropriate exit codes.\n\n### High-Level Architecture\n\n```mermaid\ngraph LR\n    CLI[\"CLI Entry Point<br/>validate-yaml.ts\"] --> ArgParser[\"Argument Parsing<br/>(process.argv)\"]\n    ArgParser --> FileReader[\"File Reader<br/>(Bun.file API)\"]\n    FileReader --> Validator[\"YAML Validator<br/>yaml-validator.ts\"]\n    Validator --> Reporter[\"Result Reporter<br/>(stdout/stderr)\"]\n    Reporter --> ExitCode[\"Exit Code<br/>(process.exit)\"]\n```\n\nThe design follows the existing project pattern of a dedicated entry point file that imports pure utility functions from a separate module.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Architecture\n\n### Component Architecture\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TB\n    subgraph \"CLI Layer\"\n        VY[\"src/validate-yaml.ts<br/>Entry Point\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"Logic Layer\"\n        YV[\"src/yaml-validator.ts<br/>Pure Functions\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"Test Layer\"\n        YVT[\"src/yaml-validator.test.ts<br/>Unit Tests\"]\n    end\n\n    VY -->|imports| YV\n    YVT -->|imports| YV\n```\n\n### Component Responsibilities\n\n| Component | File | Responsibility |\n|-----------|------|----------------|\n| CLI Entry Point | `src/validate-yaml.ts` | Argument parsing, file reading, output formatting, exit codes |\n| YAML Validator | `src/yaml-validator.ts` | Pure YAML syntax validation logic, error reporting structures |\n| Tests | `src/yaml-validator.test.ts` | Unit tests for all validator functions |\n\n### Sequence Diagram -- Validation Flow\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant User\n    participant CLI as validate-yaml.ts\n    participant FS as Bun.file API\n    participant Val as yaml-validator.ts\n\n    User->>CLI: bun run validate <filepath>\n    CLI->>CLI: Parse process.argv[2]\n\n    alt No argument provided\n        CLI->>User: stderr: Usage message\n        CLI->>CLI: process.exit(1)\n    end\n\n    CLI->>FS: Bun.file(filepath).exists()\n\n    alt File not found\n        CLI->>User: stderr: \"File not found: <path>\"\n        CLI->>CLI: process.exit(1)\n    end\n\n    FS-->>CLI: file content (string)\n    CLI->>Val: validateYaml(content)\n    Val-->>CLI: ValidationResult\n\n    alt Valid YAML\n        CLI->>User: stdout: \"Valid YAML: <filepath>\"\n        CLI->>CLI: process.exit(0)\n    else Invalid YAML\n        CLI->>User: stderr: Error description with context\n        CLI->>CLI: process.exit(1)\n    end\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. Detailed Design\n\n### 3.1 Data Model\n\n```typescript\n/** Result of YAML validation */\ninterface ValidationResult {\n  valid: boolean;\n  errors: ValidationError[];\n}\n\n/** A single validation error with location context */\ninterface ValidationError {\n  line: number;\n  column: number;\n  message: string;\n}\n```\n\n### 3.2 YAML Validator Module (`src/yaml-validator.ts`)\n\nExports:\n\n| Function | Signature | Purpose |\n|----------|-----------|---------|\n| `validateYaml` | `(content: string) => ValidationResult` | Main entry point -- validates YAML string |\n\nInternal logic (not exported, but key design elements):\n\nThe validator uses a line-based parsing approach to check YAML syntax. This approach prioritizes detecting the most common syntax errors found in configuration files rather than implementing a full YAML 1.2 specification parser.\n\n**Validation checks performed (ordered by parsing phase)**:\n\n1. **Empty document handling**: Empty string or whitespace-only content is valid YAML (BR-003).\n2. **Character validation**: Reject tabs used for indentation (YAML forbids tabs for indentation).\n3. **Indentation consistency**: Verify that indentation uses consistent space increments and that nested blocks are properly indented relative to their parent.\n4. **Quote matching**: Detect unclosed single or double quotes within scalar values.\n5. **Flow collection matching**: Detect unmatched `[`/`]` and `{`/`}` brackets for inline flow-style sequences and mappings.\n6. **Mapping syntax**: Validate that mapping entries have the form `key: value` (colon followed by space or end-of-line) when on a non-sequence line.\n7. **Sequence syntax**: Validate list items begin with `- ` (dash followed by space) at appropriate indentation levels.\n8. **Document markers**: Recognize `---` and `...` as valid document boundary markers.\n9. **Comment handling**: Lines starting with `#` (with optional leading whitespace) and inline comments (` #`) are valid and skipped.\n10. **Multi-line scalar indicators**: Recognize `|` and `>` (with optional modifiers like `|+`, `|-`, `>-`) as block scalar indicators.\n\n**Known limitations (by design, per scope)**:\n- No support for multi-document streams (only first document validated).\n- No anchor/alias resolution (`&` and `*` references).\n- No tag resolution (`!!str`, `!!int`, etc.) -- tags are accepted syntactically but not validated.\n- No schema validation.\n\n### 3.3 CLI Entry Point (`src/validate-yaml.ts`)\n\nExecution flow:\n\n1. Read `process.argv[2]` for file path.\n2. If no argument: print usage to stderr, exit 1.\n3. Create `Bun.file(filepath)` reference.\n4. Check existence via `.exists()`. If not found: print \"File not found: {path}\" to stderr, exit 1.\n5. Read content via `.text()` in a try/catch. If read fails: print permission/read error to stderr, exit 1.\n6. Call `validateYaml(content)`.\n7. If `result.valid`: print \"Valid YAML: {filepath}\" to stdout, exit 0.\n8. If not valid: print error details to stderr (including line number and description), exit 1.\n\n**Usage message format**:\n```\nUsage: bun run validate <filepath>\n\nValidates a YAML file for syntactic correctness.\n```\n\n**Error output format**:\n```\nYAML validation error in <filepath>:\n  Line <N>, Column <M>: <error description>\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. Technology Stack\n\n| Category | Choice | Rationale |\n|----------|--------|-----------|\n| Runtime | Bun | Existing project runtime |\n| Language | TypeScript (strict mode) | Existing project language |\n| File I/O | `Bun.file()` API | Bun-native, async-capable file reading |\n| CLI args | `process.argv` | Existing pattern in `src/index.ts` |\n| Testing | `bun:test` | Existing project test framework |\n| Dependencies | None new | Hard constraint FR-006 / BR-001 |\n\n---\n\n## 5. Implementation Plan\n\n| # | Component | Description | Files Modified/Created |\n|---|-----------|-------------|----------------------|\n| T1 | YAML Validator Module | Core validation logic -- pure functions implementing line-based YAML syntax checking. Types `ValidationResult` and `ValidationError`. Main export `validateYaml()`. | Create: `src/yaml-validator.ts` |\n| T2 | CLI Entry Point | Script that reads CLI args, reads file via Bun.file, calls validator, formats output, sets exit code. | Create: `src/validate-yaml.ts` |\n| T3 | Unit Tests | Tests for `validateYaml()` covering: valid YAML (basic mapping, sequences, nested, empty), invalid YAML (bad indentation, unclosed quotes, malformed mappings, unmatched brackets), and edge cases (empty file, comments-only, document markers). | Create: `src/yaml-validator.test.ts` |\n| T4 | Package.json Script | Add `\"validate\"` script entry pointing to `bun run src/validate-yaml.ts`. | Modify: `package.json` |\n\n---\n\n## 6. Implementation DAG\n\n**Parallel Groups** (tasks with no inter-dependencies):\n\n1. [T1] - Foundation module with no dependencies on other new components\n2. [T2, T3] - Both depend only on T1; CLI entry and tests are independent of each other\n3. [T4] - Package.json update references the CLI entry point from T2\n\n**Dependencies**:\n\n- T2 -> T1 (Interface: CLI imports `validateYaml` from yaml-validator module)\n- T3 -> T1 (Interface: Tests import `validateYaml` from yaml-validator module)\n- T4 -> T2 (Build: Script entry references `src/validate-yaml.ts`)\n\n**Critical Path**: T1 -> T2 -> T4\n\n---\n\n## 7. Testing Strategy\n\n### Test Value Assessment\n\n| Test Category | Value | Rationale |\n|---------------|-------|-----------|\n| Valid YAML acceptance | HIGH | Core business logic -- must correctly identify well-formed YAML |\n| Invalid YAML rejection with errors | HIGH | Core business logic -- must detect and report syntax errors |\n| Empty file handling | MEDIUM | Business rule BR-003 explicit requirement |\n| Edge cases (comments, markers) | MEDIUM | App-specific parsing correctness |\n| CLI argument handling | LOW | Thin wrapper; tested via integration if needed |\n| File reading errors | LOW | Bun.file API behavior; light smoke test sufficient |\n\n### Test Plan (`src/yaml-validator.test.ts`)\n\nTests target the `validateYaml` function (pure function, easy to unit test).\n\n**Valid YAML cases**:\n- Simple key-value mapping (`key: value`)\n- Nested mappings (indented blocks)\n- Sequences (list items with `- `)\n- Mixed mappings and sequences\n- Quoted strings (single and double)\n- Empty content (BR-003)\n- Comment-only files\n- Document markers (`---`, `...`)\n- Multi-line scalars (`|`, `>`)\n- Flow-style collections (`[a, b]`, `{a: 1}`)\n\n**Invalid YAML cases**:\n- Tab indentation\n- Unclosed double quote\n- Unclosed single quote\n- Inconsistent indentation\n- Malformed mapping (missing space after colon in ambiguous context)\n- Unmatched opening bracket `[`\n- Unmatched opening brace `{`\n- Unmatched closing bracket `]`\n- Unmatched closing brace `}`\n\n**Edge cases**:\n- Whitespace-only file\n- Single-line file\n- File with only `---`\n- Colon in quoted string (should be valid)\n- Hash in quoted string (should be valid, not a comment)\n\n### Tests NOT included (per test value assessment):\n- Bun.file() read behavior verification\n- process.argv parsing framework behavior\n- process.exit() call verification\n\n---\n\n## 8. Deployment Design\n\nNo special deployment required. The feature integrates into the existing project structure.\n\n| Aspect | Detail |\n|--------|--------|\n| Invocation | `bun run validate <filepath>` |\n| Script entry | `package.json` -> `\"validate\": \"bun run src/validate-yaml.ts\"` |\n| Runtime requirement | Bun (already present) |\n| Build step | None (Bun runs TypeScript directly) |\n| Environment variables | None |\n\n---\n\n## 9. Documentation Impact\n\n| Type | Target | Section | KB Source | Rationale |\n|------|--------|---------|-----------|-----------|\n| edit | `.rp1/context/index.md` | Project Structure | index.md:Project Structure | New files added to `src/` |\n| edit | `.rp1/context/modules.md` | Modules | modules.md:Modules | Two new modules: yaml-validator, validate-yaml |\n| edit | `.rp1/context/architecture.md` | Scripts | architecture.md:Scripts | New `validate` script added |\n\n---\n\n## 10. Design Decisions Log\n\n| ID | Decision | Choice | Rationale | Alternatives Considered |\n|----|----------|--------|-----------|------------------------|\n| D1 | YAML parsing approach | Custom line-based syntax validator | Zero-dependency constraint forbids npm packages; Bun has no built-in YAML parser; line-based approach is sufficient for syntax checking | Full recursive descent parser (too complex for scope), regex-only approach (insufficient for nested structures) |\n| D2 | Module structure | Separate validator module + CLI entry point | Follows existing pattern (utils.ts + index.ts separation); enables unit testing of pure validation logic | Single file (violates separation of concerns), adding to existing utils.ts (unrelated functionality) |\n| D3 | File reading API | `Bun.file()` API | Native Bun API, aligns with zero-dependency constraint, async-capable | Node.js `fs.readFileSync` (works but not Bun-idiomatic), `fs.promises.readFile` (also works, less idiomatic) |\n| D4 | Entry point file name | `src/validate-yaml.ts` | kebab-case per project pattern; descriptive of purpose; mirrors `index.ts` as a runnable script | `src/cli.ts` (too generic), `src/yaml-cli.ts` (less descriptive) |\n| D5 | Error reporting granularity | Line and column numbers with description | Requirements specify \"actionable feedback\" and \"nature of the error\"; line/column enables quick navigation | Message-only (less actionable), AST-based (over-engineered for syntax check) |\n| D6 | YAML spec coverage | Common config-file subset of YAML 1.2 | Requirements specify \"simple\" tool for config files; full spec is thousands of pages and impractical without a library | Full YAML 1.2 (impractical without deps), YAML 1.1 (same issue), JSON-only subset (too restrictive) |\n"
