        "old_string": "## Validation Findings\n",
        "new_string": "## Validation Findings\n\n### HYP-001 Findings\n**Validated**: 2026-03-08T04:24:00Z\n**Method**: CODE_EXPERIMENT + EXTERNAL_RESEARCH\n**Result**: REJECTED\n\n**Evidence**:\n\nBun (v1.2.21+) introduced built-in YAML support as a first-class feature. The installed Bun version (1.3.3) fully supports this API. Testing confirmed:\n\n1. **`Bun.YAML` global object exists** -- `typeof Bun.YAML` returns `\"object\"` with `parse` and `stringify` methods.\n\n2. **`Bun.YAML.parse()` works correctly** -- Parses YAML strings into JavaScript objects:\n   ```\n   Bun.YAML.parse(\"name: test\\nversion: 1.0\\nitems:\\n  - a\\n  - b\")\n   // => { name: \"test\", version: 1, items: [\"a\", \"b\"] }\n   ```\n\n3. **`import { YAML } from \"bun\"` works** -- The YAML parser is also accessible via ES module import:\n   ```\n   import { YAML } from \"bun\";\n   YAML.parse(\"hello: world\") // => { hello: \"world\" }\n   ```\n\n4. **Direct `.yaml` file import works** -- Bun can import YAML files as modules:\n   ```\n   import config from \"./sample.yaml\";\n   // config is a parsed JavaScript object\n   ```\n\n5. **Multi-document support** -- `Bun.YAML.parse()` returns an array when parsing multi-document YAML (separated by `---`).\n\n6. **Error handling** -- Invalid YAML throws `SyntaxError` with a descriptive message (e.g., \"YAML Parse error: Unexpected EOF\", \"YAML Parse error: Unexpected token\").\n\n7. **Error detail limitation** -- The thrown `SyntaxError` does NOT include YAML-content line/column numbers. The `line` and `column` properties on the error refer to the JavaScript call site, not the position within the YAML content. Properties `originalLine` and `originalColumn` are `undefined`.\n\n8. **Parsing leniency** -- `Bun.YAML.parse()` accepts some technically invalid YAML without error: tab indentation produces a parsed result (treats tab as key separator rather than indentation), and duplicate keys silently use the last value.\n\n9. **`Bun.YAML.stringify()` exists** -- Converting JS objects back to YAML is also available.\n\n10. **YAML 1.2 spec coverage** -- Bun's parser passes over 90% of the official YAML test suite, with support for anchors, aliases, tags, multi-line scalars, and directives.\n\n**Sources**:\n- https://bun.com/docs/api/yaml (Bun YAML API documentation)\n- https://bun.com/docs/runtime/yaml (Bun YAML runtime support documentation)\n- https://github.com/oven-sh/bun/issues/1003 (Original feature request for built-in YAML support)\n- https://www.theregister.com/2025/08/27/bun_js_toolkit_adds_mysql/ (Bun v1.2.21 release coverage)\n- Code experiments in `/tmp/hypothesis-yaml-validator-command/` (4 test scripts executed)\n\n**Implications for Design**:\n\nThe design assumes a custom line-based YAML syntax validator is necessary (Design Decision D1). This assumption is incorrect -- `Bun.YAML.parse()` provides a built-in, high-performance Zig-based YAML parser that covers YAML 1.2 spec with >90% test suite compliance. The design has two viable paths:\n\n1. **Use `Bun.YAML.parse()` as the validator**: Replace the custom parser with a simple try/catch around `Bun.YAML.parse()`. This satisfies the zero-dependency constraint (it is a Bun built-in) and provides far more complete YAML spec coverage than a hand-written parser. However, error messages from `Bun.YAML.parse()` lack line/column context within the YAML content, which conflicts with the design's requirement for \"actionable feedback\" with line/column numbers (Design Decision D5).\n\n2. **Hybrid approach**: Use `Bun.YAML.parse()` for primary validation (valid/invalid determination) and supplement with a lightweight custom line scanner only for error location reporting when `Bun.YAML.parse()` throws.\n\n3. **Keep custom parser**: If precise line/column error reporting is the primary goal, a custom parser may still be warranted, but the rationale in D1 (\"Bun has no built-in YAML parser\") must be updated to reflect the actual reason (error granularity, not absence of parser).\n\n## Summary\n| Hypothesis | Risk | Result | Implication |\n|------------|------|--------|-------------|\n| HYP-001 | HIGH | REJECTED | Bun provides built-in `Bun.YAML.parse()` since v1.2.21; design decision D1 rationale is invalid; custom parser may still be warranted for line/column error reporting but not for lack of a built-in parser |\n"
