        "content": "# Development Tasks: YAML Validator Command\n\n**Feature ID**: yaml-validator-command\n**Status**: Not Started\n**Progress**: 0% (0 of 7 tasks)\n**Estimated Effort**: 1 day\n**Started**: 2026-03-08\n\n## Overview\n\nA CLI command that validates YAML files for syntactic correctness, implemented as a thin wrapper around `Bun.YAML.parse()`. The tool reads a file path from CLI arguments, attempts to parse the content, and reports success or failure with appropriate exit codes. The validator module is separated from the CLI entry point following the project's existing pattern of pure utility functions imported by dedicated entry point scripts.\n\n## Implementation DAG\n\n**Parallel Groups** (tasks with no inter-dependencies):\n\n1. [T1] - Foundation module with no dependencies on other new components\n2. [T2, T3] - Both depend only on T1; CLI entry and tests are independent of each other\n3. [T4] - Package.json update references the CLI entry point from T2\n\n**Dependencies**:\n\n- T2 -> T1 (Interface: CLI imports `validateYaml` from yaml-validator module)\n- T3 -> T1 (Interface: Tests import `validateYaml` from yaml-validator module)\n- T4 -> T2 (Build: Script entry references `src/validate-yaml.ts`)\n\n**Critical Path**: T1 -> T2 -> T4\n\n## Task Breakdown\n\n### Foundation\n\n- [ ] **T1**: Create YAML validator module wrapping `Bun.YAML.parse()` with structured result interface `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#32-yaml-validator-module](design.md#32-yaml-validator-module)\n\n    **Effort**: 1 hour\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] File `src/yaml-validator.ts` is created\n    - [ ] Exports `ValidationResult` interface with `valid: boolean` and optional `error?: string`\n    - [ ] Exports `validateYaml(content: string): ValidationResult` function\n    - [ ] Empty string and whitespace-only input returns `{ valid: true }` without calling the parser (BR-003)\n    - [ ] Valid YAML content returns `{ valid: true }` after successful `Bun.YAML.parse()` call\n    - [ ] `SyntaxError` thrown by parser is caught and returned as `{ valid: false, error: error.message }`\n    - [ ] Non-SyntaxError exceptions are caught and returned as `{ valid: false, error: \"Unexpected error: ...\" }`\n\n### CLI and Testing\n\n- [ ] **T2**: Create CLI entry point script with argument parsing, file reading, output formatting, and exit codes `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#33-cli-entry-point](design.md#33-cli-entry-point)\n\n    **Effort**: 2 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] File `src/validate-yaml.ts` is created\n    - [ ] Reads file path from `process.argv[2]`\n    - [ ] Prints usage message to stderr and exits with code 1 when no argument is provided (FR-001)\n    - [ ] Prints \"File not found: {path}\" to stderr and exits with code 1 when file does not exist (FR-005)\n    - [ ] Prints permission/read error to stderr and exits with code 1 when file cannot be read (FR-005)\n    - [ ] Prints \"Valid YAML: {filepath}\" to stdout and exits with code 0 for valid YAML (FR-003, FR-004)\n    - [ ] Prints formatted error message to stderr and exits with code 1 for invalid YAML (FR-003, FR-004)\n    - [ ] Uses `Bun.file()` API for file operations (no new dependencies)\n    - [ ] Imports `validateYaml` from `yaml-validator.ts`\n\n- [ ] **T3**: Create unit tests for the `validateYaml` wrapper function `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#7-testing-strategy](design.md#7-testing-strategy)\n\n    **Effort**: 2 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] File `src/yaml-validator.test.ts` is created\n    - [ ] Tests use `bun:test` framework\n    - [ ] Valid YAML cases tested: simple key-value, nested mappings, sequences, mixed mappings and sequences\n    - [ ] Empty content returns `{ valid: true }` (BR-003)\n    - [ ] Whitespace-only content returns `{ valid: true }` (BR-003)\n    - [ ] Invalid YAML cases tested: unclosed flow collection, malformed mapping structure\n    - [ ] Verifies `error` field is a non-empty string when validation fails\n    - [ ] Verifies `error` field is undefined when validation succeeds\n    - [ ] Verifies `valid` field is boolean in all cases\n    - [ ] All tests pass via `bun test`\n\n### Integration\n\n- [ ] **T4**: Add `validate` script entry to `package.json` `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#8-deployment-design](design.md#8-deployment-design)\n\n    **Effort**: 30 minutes\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] `package.json` contains script entry `\"validate\": \"bun run src/validate-yaml.ts\"`\n    - [ ] `bun run validate <filepath>` successfully invokes the validator\n    - [ ] No new dependencies added to `package.json` (FR-006, BR-001)\n\n### User Docs\n\n- [ ] **TD1**: Update `.rp1/context/index.md` - Project Structure `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#documentation-impact](design.md#documentation-impact)\n\n    **Type**: edit\n\n    **Target**: `.rp1/context/index.md`\n\n    **Section**: Project Structure\n\n    **KB Source**: index.md:Project Structure\n\n    **Effort**: 30 minutes\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] Section reflects new files `src/yaml-validator.ts`, `src/validate-yaml.ts`, and `src/yaml-validator.test.ts`\n\n- [ ] **TD2**: Update `.rp1/context/modules.md` - Modules `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#documentation-impact](design.md#documentation-impact)\n\n    **Type**: edit\n\n    **Target**: `.rp1/context/modules.md`\n\n    **Section**: Modules\n\n    **KB Source**: modules.md:Modules\n\n    **Effort**: 30 minutes\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] Section includes documentation for the `yaml-validator` module (exports, purpose)\n    - [ ] Section includes documentation for the `validate-yaml` CLI entry point (purpose, usage)\n\n- [ ] **TD3**: Update `.rp1/context/architecture.md` - Scripts `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#documentation-impact](design.md#documentation-impact)\n\n    **Type**: edit\n\n    **Target**: `.rp1/context/architecture.md`\n\n    **Section**: Scripts\n\n    **KB Source**: architecture.md:Scripts\n\n    **Effort**: 30 minutes\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] Section documents the new `validate` script and its invocation pattern\n\n## Acceptance Criteria Checklist\n\n- [ ] Valid YAML files are correctly identified as valid (100% of well-formed YAML accepted)\n- [ ] Invalid YAML files are correctly rejected with meaningful error messages\n- [ ] Zero new dependencies added to `package.json` (FR-006, BR-001)\n- [ ] Command execution completes in sub-second time for files under 10KB\n- [ ] Exit code 0 for valid YAML, exit code 1 for invalid/error (FR-004)\n- [ ] Usage message displayed when no arguments provided (FR-001)\n- [ ] \"File not found\" error for missing files (FR-005)\n- [ ] Empty files treated as valid YAML (BR-003)\n- [ ] Command invocable via `bun run validate <filepath>` (FR-007)\n- [ ] Error messages printed to stderr, success messages to stdout (FR-003)\n- [ ] Only local files accessed; no writes or modifications (security requirement)\n\n## Definition of Done\n\n- [ ] All tasks completed\n- [ ] All AC verified\n- [ ] Code reviewed\n- [ ] Docs updated\n"
