        "content": "# Development Tasks: YAML Validator Command\n\n**Feature ID**: yaml-validator-command\n**Status**: Not Started\n**Progress**: 0% (0 of 7 tasks)\n**Estimated Effort**: 2 days\n**Started**: 2026-03-08\n\n## Overview\n\nA lightweight CLI command that validates YAML files for syntactic correctness. The command accepts a file path argument, reads the file, runs it through a hand-written YAML syntax validator, and reports the result with appropriate exit codes. Introduces two new source files (`src/yaml-validator.ts` and `src/validate-yaml.ts`), a test file, and a `package.json` script entry. No new dependencies.\n\n## Implementation DAG\n\n**Parallel Groups** (tasks with no inter-dependencies):\n\n1. [T1] - Core validation module has no dependencies on other new components\n2. [T2, T3] - Both depend on T1 interfaces but are independent of each other\n3. [T4] - Script entry references T2's file path\n\n**Dependencies**:\n\n- T2 -> T1 (Interface: T2 imports `validateYaml` from T1)\n- T3 -> T1 (Interface: T3 imports `validateYaml` from T1 for testing)\n- T4 -> T2 (Build: script entry references T2's file path)\n\n**Critical Path**: T1 -> T2 -> T4\n\n## Task Breakdown\n\n### Core Validation Module\n\n- [ ] **T1**: Implement the `validateYaml()` function and type definitions (`ValidationResult`, `ValidationError`) in `src/yaml-validator.ts` `[complexity:medium]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#32-core-validation-logic-srcyaml-validatorts](design.md#32-core-validation-logic-srcyaml-validatorts)\n\n    **Effort**: 6 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] `ValidationError` interface exported with `line` (number) and `message` (string) fields\n    - [ ] `ValidationResult` interface exported with `valid` (boolean) and `errors` (ValidationError[]) fields\n    - [ ] `validateYaml(content: string): ValidationResult` function exported\n    - [ ] Detects tab indentation and reports the offending line number\n    - [ ] Detects unclosed single and double quoted strings\n    - [ ] Detects mismatched flow indicators (`[]` and `{}`)\n    - [ ] Detects invalid mapping syntax (missing colon separator)\n    - [ ] Detects inconsistent indentation levels\n    - [ ] Validates document markers (`---` and `...`) usage\n    - [ ] Skips comment lines and blank lines during validation\n    - [ ] Returns `{ valid: true, errors: [] }` for empty and whitespace-only input\n    - [ ] Processes input line-by-line\n    - [ ] No external dependencies used -- only TypeScript and Bun built-ins\n\n### CLI Entry Point and Tests\n\n- [ ] **T2**: Implement the CLI entry point in `src/validate-yaml.ts` with argument parsing, file reading, output formatting, and exit code logic `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#33-cli-entry-point-srcvalidate-yamlts](design.md#33-cli-entry-point-srcvalidate-yamlts)\n\n    **Effort**: 2 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] Reads file path from `process.argv[2]`\n    - [ ] Prints usage message to stderr and exits with code 1 when no argument provided\n    - [ ] Reads file contents using `Bun.file(path).text()`\n    - [ ] Prints `Valid YAML: <filepath>` to stdout and exits with code 0 for valid YAML\n    - [ ] Prints `Invalid YAML: <filepath>` followed by `  Line <N>: <error message>` per error to stderr and exits with code 1 for invalid YAML\n    - [ ] Prints `Error: File not found: <filepath>` to stderr and exits with code 1 when file does not exist\n    - [ ] Prints `Error: Cannot read file: <filepath>` to stderr and exits with code 1 when file is unreadable\n    - [ ] Imports `validateYaml` from `./yaml-validator`\n\n- [ ] **T3**: Write unit tests in `src/yaml-validator.test.ts` covering valid YAML, each syntax error type, edge cases, and error result structure `[complexity:medium]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#7-testing-strategy](design.md#7-testing-strategy)\n\n    **Effort**: 4 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] Test file uses `bun:test` framework with `describe`/`test`/`expect` pattern\n    - [ ] Tests valid YAML: simple key-value pair returns `{ valid: true, errors: [] }`\n    - [ ] Tests valid YAML: nested mapping with multi-level indentation\n    - [ ] Tests valid YAML: list items (`- item1\\n- item2`)\n    - [ ] Tests valid YAML: comments and blank lines interspersed with content\n    - [ ] Tests valid YAML: empty input returns `{ valid: true, errors: [] }`\n    - [ ] Tests valid YAML: flow-style collections (`items: [a, b, c]`)\n    - [ ] Tests invalid YAML: tab indentation detected with correct line number\n    - [ ] Tests invalid YAML: unclosed double quote detected\n    - [ ] Tests invalid YAML: unclosed single quote detected\n    - [ ] Tests invalid YAML: mismatched brackets (`[`) detected\n    - [ ] Tests invalid YAML: mismatched braces (`{`) detected\n    - [ ] Tests edge case: whitespace-only input returns `{ valid: true, errors: [] }`\n    - [ ] Tests edge case: document markers (`---`, `...`) accepted as valid\n    - [ ] All tests pass when run via `bun test`\n\n### Package Integration\n\n- [ ] **T4**: Add `validate-yaml` script entry to `package.json` pointing to `bun run src/validate-yaml.ts` `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#34-packagejson-update](design.md#34-packagejson-update)\n\n    **Effort**: 15 minutes\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] `package.json` contains `\"validate-yaml\": \"bun run src/validate-yaml.ts\"` in the `scripts` section\n    - [ ] No new entries added to `dependencies` or `devDependencies`\n    - [ ] Running `bun run validate-yaml <filepath>` invokes the validator\n\n### User Docs\n\n- [ ] **TD1**: Update modules.md - Modules `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#documentation-impact](design.md#documentation-impact)\n\n    **Type**: edit\n\n    **Target**: `.rp1/context/modules.md`\n\n    **Section**: Modules\n\n    **KB Source**: modules.md\n\n    **Effort**: 30 minutes\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] `yaml-validator.ts` module documented with its purpose and exported function\n    - [ ] `validate-yaml.ts` module documented with its purpose as CLI entry point\n    - [ ] Section reflects the validation module's relationship to the CLI entry point\n\n- [ ] **TD2**: Update architecture.md - Scripts `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#documentation-impact](design.md#documentation-impact)\n\n    **Type**: edit\n\n    **Target**: `.rp1/context/architecture.md`\n\n    **Section**: Scripts\n\n    **KB Source**: architecture.md\n\n    **Effort**: 30 minutes\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] `validate-yaml` script listed in the scripts section\n    - [ ] Script description matches its purpose (YAML syntax validation CLI)\n\n- [ ] **TD3**: Update index.md - Project Structure `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#documentation-impact](design.md#documentation-impact)\n\n    **Type**: edit\n\n    **Target**: `.rp1/context/index.md`\n\n    **Section**: Project Structure\n\n    **KB Source**: index.md\n\n    **Effort**: 30 minutes\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] `src/yaml-validator.ts` listed in the project structure diagram\n    - [ ] `src/validate-yaml.ts` listed in the project structure diagram\n    - [ ] `src/yaml-validator.test.ts` listed in the project structure diagram\n\n## Acceptance Criteria Checklist\n\n- [ ] REQ-001 AC-1: Running the command with a valid file path reads and processes that file\n- [ ] REQ-001 AC-2: Running the command without a file path argument produces a usage message explaining expected input\n- [ ] REQ-002 AC-1: A file containing valid YAML produces a success message\n- [ ] REQ-002 AC-2: A file containing invalid YAML produces an error message describing the problem\n- [ ] REQ-003 AC-1: On success, a message confirming validity is printed to stdout\n- [ ] REQ-003 AC-2: On failure, an error message is printed to stderr that includes a description of the syntax error\n- [ ] REQ-004 AC-1: Exit code is