        "content": "# Design Decisions: YAML Validator Command\n\n**Feature ID**: yaml-validator-command\n**Created**: 2026-03-08\n\n## Decision Log\n\n| ID | Decision | Choice | Rationale | Alternatives Considered |\n|----|----------|--------|-----------|------------------------|\n| D1 | YAML parsing approach | Hand-written line-by-line syntax validator | No-new-deps constraint (REQ-006) prohibits adding a YAML parsing library. Bun does not include a built-in YAML parser. A hand-written validator targeting common syntax errors is sufficient for the syntax-only scope. | (a) Use `js-yaml` npm package -- rejected due to no-new-deps constraint. (b) Port a subset of a YAML parser -- rejected as overly complex for the scope. (c) Use regex-only validation -- rejected as too fragile for structured syntax. |\n| D2 | File structure pattern | Separate CLI entry point (`validate-yaml.ts`) + pure utility module (`yaml-validator.ts`) | Follows existing `index.ts` + `utils.ts` separation pattern. Keeps validation logic testable as pure functions without CLI coupling. | (a) Single file with both CLI and logic -- rejected as inconsistent with existing codebase pattern and harder to test. (b) Add validation to existing `utils.ts` -- rejected as unrelated to existing utils; would bloat that module. |\n| D3 | Error reporting format | Structured `ValidationResult` type with `valid` boolean and `errors` array | Provides machine-readable results that the CLI layer can format for human output. Enables testing of specific error details. Follows TypeScript strict mode patterns. | (a) Throw exceptions for invalid YAML -- rejected as validation failures are expected outcomes, not exceptional conditions. (b) Return simple boolean -- rejected as insufficient for error reporting (REQ-003 requires error details). |\n| D4 | File I/O API | `Bun.file(path).text()` | Bun-native API, consistent with using the Bun runtime. Returns a promise for async file reading. Throws on missing/unreadable files which aligns with the try/catch error handling pattern. | (a) `node:fs` `readFileSync` -- rejected as synchronous and less idiomatic for Bun. (b) `node:fs/promises` `readFile` -- viable but Bun.file() is more idiomatic. |\n| D5 | Script naming | `validate-yaml` | Follows kebab-case naming convention from patterns.md. Descriptive and consistent with existing script names (`dev`, `test`, `lint`, `format`). | (a) `yaml-validate` -- rejected as less natural English phrasing. (b) `check-yaml` -- viable but \"validate\" more precisely describes the action. |\n| D6 | Test co-location | `src/yaml-validator.test.ts` alongside `src/yaml-validator.ts` | Follows existing pattern where `utils.test.ts` is co-located with `utils.ts`. Consistent with patterns.md and tsconfig.json include paths. | (a) Separate `tests/` directory -- rejected as inconsistent with existing codebase pattern. |\n| D7 | Exit code scheme | 0 for valid, 1 for all errors (invalid YAML, missing file, usage error) | Simple and standard. Consistent with Unix conventions. CI pipelines only need zero vs non-zero distinction. | (a) Different codes per error type (1=invalid, 2=file error, 3=usage) -- rejected as over-engineering for this scope; no requirement distinguishes error types by exit code. |\n\n## AFK Mode: Auto-Selected Technology Decisions\n\n| Decision | Choice | Source | Rationale |\n|----------|--------|--------|-----------|\n| Language | TypeScript (strict mode) | KB: patterns.md | Only language used in project |\n| Runtime | Bun | KB: index.md | Only runtime used in project |\n| Test framework | bun:test | KB: patterns.md | Only test framework used in project |\n| File I/O | Bun.file() | Codebase pattern | Bun-idiomatic file reading |\n| Module style | ESM | KB: patterns.md | Project uses `\"type\": \"module\"` |\n| File naming | kebab-case | KB: patterns.md | Established naming convention |\n| Function naming | camelCase | KB: patterns.md | Established naming convention |\n| Type naming | PascalCase | KB: patterns.md | Established naming convention |\n| Error handling | try/catch with descriptive messages | KB: patterns.md | Established error handling pattern |\n| YAML parsing | Hand-written validator | Constraint: REQ-006 | No new dependencies allowed; Bun has no built-in YAML parser |\n"
