        "content": "# Hypothesis Document: yaml-validator-command\n**Version**: 1.0.0 | **Created**: 2026-03-08T15:23:00Z | **Status**: PENDING\n\n## Hypotheses\n### HYP-001: Hand-written line-by-line YAML syntax validator feasibility\n**Risk Level**: HIGH\n**Status**: PENDING\n**Statement**: A hand-written, line-by-line YAML syntax validator can reliably detect the most common YAML syntax errors (tab indentation, unclosed quotes, mismatched flow indicators, inconsistent indentation) without implementing a full spec-compliant parser.\n**Context**: The design proposes building a lightweight YAML validator as a CLI command. If a line-by-line approach cannot handle common YAML patterns correctly, the design must either adopt a full parser or significantly narrow the scope of validation.\n**Validation Criteria**:\n- CONFIRM if: A prototype validator correctly identifies validity/invalidity for a corpus of 20+ representative YAML files including nested mappings, flow collections, multi-line strings, anchors/aliases, and common error patterns.\n- REJECT if: The prototype fails on more than 10% of common YAML patterns (e.g., incorrectly rejects valid multi-line scalars, block scalars with | or >, or correctly-indented complex nested structures).\n**Suggested Method**: CODE_EXPERIMENT\n\n## Validation Findings\n"
